Phase 29 — break test for the sequence half of page-inflight-check
==================================================================

Taken in the chat session's own sandbox, 2026-08-12, chromium-1194.
`bash scripts/break-page-inflight-sequence.sh`, run three times; the third is
below, and what the first two changed is recorded underneath it.

Each variant reintroduces one defect into the PAGE (or into the instrument),
rebuilds site/index.html, and requires the gate to say so. Exit status is taken
from the gate directly, never through a pipe.

[D] IS THE ONE WORTH READING TWICE. It reverts the idle interval to the constant
and the gate answers `(285s, 300s]`. Phase 28 measured 293 s on `destroy prod
#46`, live, against the same ceiling. The fixture reproduces the finding to
within one step of the walk, which is the closest this project has come to
holding one of its live findings still.

