break-page-inflight-sequence: 7 of 7 variants behaved as written.

--- WHAT THE FIRST TWO RUNS CHANGED ----------------------------------------

FIRST RUN, 6 of 7. [D] went red and the harness scored it a miss, because the
walk stopped at 150 s - one step past the 120 s ceiling - and a page on the
five-minute clock says nothing at all inside that. The gate reported

        the page still says nothing about the run 150s after it started

which is true, and is the empty result that looks like a measurement: it does
not say WHICH clock the page is on, and that is the entire content of ADR-0062
D2. The walk now runs to 330 s, far enough to catch the old constant, and the
red variant names the delay instead of reporting a silence. Virtual time makes
the extra steps free, so nothing was traded for it.

SECOND RUN, 7 of 7, and the log was worth less than the run. `check` printed
only the verdict lines, so the file recorded THAT [D] went red and not that it
went red at (285s, 300s]. The numbers are the evidence; the filter now keeps
them.

Both corrections are the same shape as the phase's subject, arriving in the
harness rather than in the page: an instrument that reads part of what it is
looking at.

--- WHAT EACH VARIANT IS FOR -----------------------------------------------

[A] control     the tree as committed, both claims green
[B] page        nodeTense()'s comparison disabled - the qualifier back on
                everything, which is the defect ADR-0062 D1 watched live
[C] page        readRunLayer() stops carrying `published_by`. A DIFFERENT
                mechanism with the same symptom, and the one the real defect
                actually had: the id was in the document and thrown away in the
                fold. A gate that only caught [B] would be watching the wrong
                half
[D] page        the idle interval back to `if (!live) return 300000`
[E] instrument  the mock stops exposing the ratelimit headers across the origin.
                Not a page defect - the defect this gate SHIPPED with, and
                without the refusal it measures the page's fallback branch and
                reports a number production never produces. Must refuse (2),
                not answer
[F] instrument  the overlay pointed at the unpublished document, so the publish
                moves nothing. The subject that never became one - the mirror of
                a control that reproduces its defect. Must refuse (2) before any
                sentence is judged
[G] control     green again, after every mutation was restored

NOT COVERED, deliberately: the sentinel that proves the page was never reloaded.
Breaking it means editing the gate's own navigation rather than the page, and a
variant that rewrites the measurement to fail is not evidence about the
measurement. It fires on a real reload; nothing here has made it do so.
